How stable are these grants?
----------------------------

All venv pythons on this host are **symlinks** to python.org's framework
Python installs under /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/*.
Those builds are signed by the Python Software Foundation with a
Developer-ID certificate, so macOS FDA records a *signature-based*
requirement rather than a cdhash, and the grant is far more durable:

  - `uv pip install` / Ansible re-runs inside the venv         → grant stable
  - a python.org series upgrade (e.g. 3.14.7 -> 3.14.8)        → grant stable
    (same TeamIdentifier; this file regenerates on each Ansible run so
    you can re-open it to confirm the current set)
  - macOS major version upgrade                                 → Apple re-signs
    /usr/sbin/cron etc. with the same identity → grant stable.

One click per Python series (3.14, 3.12) per host is permanent — no
Homebrew pin needed, and there is no brew-upgrade breakage to avoid.

Verifying grants are live
-------------------------

    sudo sqlite3 "/Library/Application Support/com.apple.TCC/TCC.db" \
      "SELECT client, auth_value FROM access \
       WHERE service='kTCCServiceSystemPolicyAllFiles';"

`auth_value = 2` means granted. Re-run this after clicking through the
list above — you should see one row per entry.
